<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n97" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀβλαβ-ής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>without harm,</i> i.e.,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>unharmed, unhurt,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Sapph.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				1.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				13.27
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>P.</u>
				8.54
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				68
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				4.1.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				342b
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζῶσαν ἀβλαβεῖ βίῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					650
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀβλαβῶς,</span>
			
				Ion.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-έως,</span>
			<i>safely,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζώειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thgn.
					1154
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔχειν</span> Dexipp.<i><span class="en">
				p.148D.
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>An.</u>
				6.19.2
			</span></i>: 
				Sup.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-έστατα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Eq.</u>
					6.1
				</span></i>
			:—<i>securely,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐδήσατο σάνδαλα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Merc.</u>
					83
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Act.
			, <i>not harming, harmless, innocent,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξυνουσία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					285
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡδοναί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					357b
				</span></i>
			, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. σπασμοί</span>”
				<i>doing no serious injury,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Epid.</u>
					1.6
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ πρὸς ἀνθρώπους ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Piet.</u>
					65
				</span></i>
			: c. gen., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τῶν πλησίον</span>
			Porph <i><span class="en">
				<u>Sent.</u>
				32
			</span></i>: c. dat., <i><span class="en">
				Eus.Mynd.
				1
			</span></i>. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ῶς,</span> c. dat., <i>without harm to,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῇ γαστρί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Metrod.
					41
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>averting</i> or <i>preventing harm,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδωρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					24.98
				</span></i>
			:—in <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				953b
			</span></i> we have the act. and pass. senses conjoined, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τοῦ δρᾶσαί τε καὶ παθεῖν.</span>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> in treaties, <i>without
				violating the terms,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀβλαβῶς σπονδαῖς ἐμμένειν,</span>
			coupled with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δικαίως</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδόλως,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				5.18
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				47
			</span></i> : so in Adj., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξύμμαχοι πιστοὶ . . καὶ ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					1.33
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
